<title>FRANCE: CYCLING-DAUPHINE LIBERE FINAL STAGE PLACINGS.</title>
<headline>CYCLING-DAUPHINE LIBERE FINAL STAGE PLACINGS.</headline>
<dateline>CHAMBERY, France 1997-06-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Leading placings in the</p>
<p>seventh and last stage of the Dauphine Libere cycling race over</p>
<p>182 kms from Briancon to Chambery on Sunday:</p>
<p> 1. Andrei Teteriuk (Kazakhstan) Lotto     four hours 36 minutes</p>
<p>nine seconds</p>
<p> 2. Davide Rebellin (Italy) Francaise des Jeux	  43 seconds</p>
<p>behind</p>
<p> 3. Francois Simon (France) Gan</p>
<p> 4. Jean-Cyril Robin (France) US Postal</p>
<p> 5. Udo Bolts (Germany) Telekom			  all same time</p>
<p> 6. Christophe Moreau (France) Festina		   1:35 behind</p>
<p> 7. Michael Boogerd (Netherlands) Rabobank		 same time</p>
<p> 8. Georg Totschnig (Austria) Telekom			     1:37</p>
<p> 9. Richard Virenque (France) Festina			     1:39</p>
<p> 10. Abraham Olano (Spain) Banesto				  2:05</p>
<p>Final overall standings:</p>
<p> 1. Bolts				 30 hours 49 minutes 58 seconds</p>
<p> 2. Olano						  12 seconds behind</p>
<p> 3. Robin								   1:42</p>
<p> 4. Boogerd								 2:00</p>
<p> 5. Teteriuk								4:09</p>
<p> 6. Simon								   4:12</p>
<p> 7. Moreau								  4:17</p>
<p> 8. Vyacheslav Yekimov (Russia) US Postal			 5:03</p>
<p> 9. Mikel Zarabeitia (Spain) Once				   6:26</p>
<p> 10. Manuel Beltran (Spain) Banesto				 7:58</p>
</text>
